const intro = `<p>This page answers the questions an engineer, an investor or a policy reader tends to ask on first meeting the Reality Code Engine (RCE), a programming language with a written specification, and RCE-JEPA, a research proposal built on it. It is written to be read top to bottom: each term is defined before it is used, and each number is cited to a paper on this site or to an outside source in the list at the end, numbered in order of first citation.</p>
<p><strong>Status, 31 October 2026, at openIE-dev/rce main <code>0c015c43</code>.</strong> Research, in draft. The language, its reference checker, its emitters, its host runtime and its proofs are public code, and every commit of main that passes continuous integration is released as binaries and a container image [[repo]]. The lift of programs from other languages has a first lifter, for a subset of Python, and a probe for one Go pattern [[repo]]. The engine that would store and reuse checked work and the RCE-JEPA proposer are designs, not built. No energy figure about RCE on this page is a wall-meter reading [[rce]].</p>`;

